<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">companion</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">companion</ansi> command lets you review and manage the
creatures bound to you through manifestation magic.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Usage ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">companion</ansi>            List all your active companions.
  <ansi fg="command">companion &lt;name&gt;</ansi>     Show detailed info for one companion.
  <ansi fg="command">companion assist &lt;name&gt;</ansi>
                       Toggle auto-assist on or off for that
                       companion. When assist is on, the
                       companion joins combat alongside you
                       automatically.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What the Display Shows ━━━</ansi>

For each companion you will see:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Name</ansi>         The creature's name and bond type
               (summoned, charmed, raised, etc.).
  <ansi fg="yellow">Condition</ansi>    A rough sense of how healthy the
               companion currently is.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Auto-assist</ansi>  Whether the companion will fight with
               you automatically.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Persistence ━━━</ansi>

Companions persist across sessions. When you log out, your
companions wait for your return. Summoned and raised
companions linger in the world until you reconnect. Charmed
companions persist as long as the magical bond holds.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Stealth Warning ━━━</ansi>

Companions give away your position. You cannot sneak
effectively while companions are present -- they will be
noticed even if you are not. Dismiss your companions
before attempting anything requiring stealth.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Death is Permanent ━━━</ansi>

If a companion falls in battle it is gone. Summon or charm
a new one to replace it. Guard your companions carefully
in dangerous areas.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help manifestation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help dismiss</ansi>
